consensus:
Researchers should become:
1. Skillful users of AI and understand its value for their fields;
2. Be knowledgeable about their own fields of research and develop a sense of purpose for their involvement in science;
3. Knowledge and research should become more focused on their institutional value and contribution to the betterment of quality of life;
4. Not all AI output is functional or non-functional - embrace this and know the difference.

Adjust the review system to exclude low-quality autoresearching; 
improve the process and logic of peer review. 
State the proportion and contribution of AI in research. Hopefully, in the future there will be a Git-like AI-assisted research record system required for submission and made public after publication.
